# __NAME__

A local KetSuite application generated with `@ketvietlab/ketsuite`.

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open `http://127.0.0.1:3000/admin/login` and sign in with `admin` / `admin`.

> The generated credentials are intentionally insecure and only enabled by the
> `--dev-admin` flag in `npm run dev`. Change the password before sharing the
> database or exposing the server. `npm start` never creates this account.

For a production-style first administrator, remove the local database and pipe a
JSON payload with a password of at least eight characters into `npm run provision`.
